  <div class="container">
    <!-- Header -->
    <h1>🔌 ESP32 Backend Integration Guide</h1>
    <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 1.125rem; margin-top: 0;">
      Connect your Rien-Prescript-Beeper to the Blue Rose backend and fetch prescripts (quotes) over Wi-Fi for display on ST7789 / E-Paper screens.
    </p>

    <!-- ========================================================================== -->
    <h2>📡 Backend API Overview</h2>

    <p>The Blue Rose backend exposes a single, elegant REST API endpoint that serves personal prescripts (quotes) in a normalized 5-point bundle:</p>

    <div class="section">
      <div class="section-header">
        <div class="section-icon">🌐</div>
        <h3 style="margin: 0;">API Base URL</h3>
      </div>
      <pre><code>https://rien-bluerose-backend.kha70929.workers.dev/</code></pre>
      <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9rem; margin: var(--spacing-md) 0 0;">
        Deployed on Cloudflare Workers. Responds with JSON payloads cached at the edge. Zero authentication required for read operations.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- ========================================================================== -->
    <h2>📋 The 5-Point Quote Payload</h2>

    <p>Every prescript (quote) from the backend contains exactly 5 canonical fields that map directly to your display zones:</p>

    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Field</th>
          <th>Type</th>
          <th>Display Zone</th>
          <th>Description</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>idx</code></td>
          <td>Integer</td>
          <td>Header (left)</td>
          <td>Unique quote identifier. Displayed as <code>#6</code>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>content</code></td>
          <td>String</td>
          <td>Body (center)</td>
          <td>The main quote text. Supports multi-line. Up to ~200 chars typical.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>specificName</code></td>
          <td>String</td>
          <td>Header (left, after #)</td>
          <td>Context / origin label. E.g., "Đàn ông thích mèo, đàn bà yêu chó".</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>effectiveDate</code></td>
          <td>String</td>
          <td>Header (right)</td>
          <td>Date or period. E.g., "2021~2023" or "2025-07".</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>containerName</code></td>
          <td>String</td>
          <td>Footer (right)</td>
          <td>Source/attribution. E.g., "Spiderum - Linh Vũ".</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>hashtagThemes</code></td>
          <td>String[]</td>
          <td>Footer (left)</td>
          <td>Array of theme tags. E.g., <code>["#Heartbroken", "#Wisdom"]</code>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>category</code></td>
          <td>String</td>
          <td>Typography (format)</td>
          <td>One of <code>"writing"</code> | <code>"music"</code> | <code>"poem"</code>. Controls text alignment (writing=justified, music/poem=left).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>context</code></td>
          <td>String (optional)</td>
          <td>Footer (optional callout)</td>
          <td>Additional context note. Display on second page or callout box.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <!-- ========================================================================== -->
    <h2>🔗 Available Endpoints</h2>

    <h3>1. Fetch Random Prescript</h3>
    <div class="endpoint">
      <div class="endpoint-header">
        <span class="badge badge-method-get">GET</span>
        <code class="endpoint-path">/api/quote/random</code>
      </div>
      <p class="endpoint-description">Returns a single random prescript from the entire collection.</p>

      <h4>Response (200 OK)</h4>
      <div class="payload-schema">
{
  "idx": 6,
  "content": "Nỗi sợ lớn nhất của một người đàn ông...",
  "specificName": "Đàn ông thích mèo, đàn bà yêu chó",
  "containerName": "Spiderum - Linh Vũ",
  "category": "writing",
  "effectiveDate": "2021~2023",
  "context": "Suy ngẫm về sự yếu lòng...",
  "hashtagThemes": ["#Heartbroken", "#Love", "#Wisdom"]
}
      </div>

      <h4>Use Cases</h4>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Initial Boot:</strong> Call on startup to seed the display with a fresh prescript.</li>
        <li><strong>Page Navigation:</strong> User presses "Next Quote" button → call this endpoint to jump to a new random quote.</li>
        <li><strong>Idle Rotation:</strong> Periodically fetch a new quote every N minutes to keep the display fresh.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <h3>2. Fetch Quote by Index</h3>
    <div class="endpoint">
      <div class="endpoint-header">
        <span class="badge badge-method-get">GET</span>
        <code class="endpoint-path">/api/quote/:idx</code>
      </div>
      <p class="endpoint-description">Returns a specific prescript by its unique <code>idx</code> identifier.</p>

      <h4>Example Request</h4>
      <pre><code>GET /api/quote/6 HTTP/1.1
Host: rien-bluerose-backend.kha70929.workers.dev</code></pre>

      <h4>Response (200 OK)</h4>
      <div class="payload-schema">
{
  "idx": 6,
  "content": "...",
  "specificName": "...",
  ...
}
      </div>

      <h4>Error Response (404 Not Found)</h4>
      <div class="payload-schema">
{
  "error": "Quote not found"
}
      </div>

      <h4>Use Cases</h4>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Direct Recall:</strong> User manually enters or recalls quote #6 → fetch by index for deterministic display.</li>
        <li><strong>Bookmarking:</strong> Store the <code>idx</code> in ESP32 EEPROM/NVS for later retrieval.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <h3>3. List All Quotes (Metadata)</h3>
    <div class="endpoint">
      <div class="endpoint-header">
        <span class="badge badge-method-get">GET</span>
        <code class="endpoint-path">/api/quotes/list</code>
      </div>
      <p class="endpoint-description">Returns a lightweight list of all quotes with minimal metadata for pagination and indexing.</p>

      <h4>Response (200 OK)</h4>
      <div class="payload-schema">
[
  {
    "id": "000101A1002AF5E9",
    "idx": 6,
    "snippet": "Nỗi sợ lớn nhất của một người đàn ông..."
  },
  {
    "id": "M-00010001A1088D80",
    "idx": 1,
    "snippet": "Static, hum, tum, needle drops..."
  },
  ...
]
      </div>

      <h4>Use Cases</h4>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Caching:</strong> Fetch once on startup, store list in ESP32 SD card or flash for offline browsing.</li>
        <li><strong>Menu Navigation:</strong> Display a scrollable list of all quotes on the screen to let user pick one.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <h3>4. Fetch Taxonomy (Categories, Tags)</h3>
    <div class="endpoint">
      <div class="endpoint-header">
        <span class="badge badge-method-get">GET</span>
        <code class="endpoint-path">/api/taxonomy</code>
      </div>
      <p class="endpoint-description">Returns schema metadata: category definitions, available tags, and container info.</p>

      <h4>Response (200 OK)</h4>
      <div class="payload-schema">
{
  "specifics": [
    {
      "id": "000301A10025228C",
      "name": "Đàn ông thích mèo, đàn bà yêu chó",
      "category": "writing",
      "container_id": "..."
    }
  ],
  "themes": [
    {
      "id": "tag_heartbroken",
      "name": "Heartbroken"
    },
    {
      "id": "tag_wisdom",
      "name": "Wisdom"
    }
  ]
}
      </div>

      <h4>Use Cases</h4>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Color Mapping:</strong> Map theme names to a color palette for display rendering.</li>
        <li><strong>Filtering:</strong> Show quotes by category or tag on a menu screen.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

