    <h2>📊 Performance & Optimization</h2>

    <div class="section">
      <h3>Network Metrics</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Payload Size:</strong> ~500–2000 bytes (typical quote).</li>
        <li><strong>Request Latency:</strong> 200–800ms (WiFi + Cloudflare edge routing).</li>
        <li><strong>Refresh Rate:</strong> Keep minimum 30–60 second intervals between fetches to avoid hammering backend.</li>
        <li><strong>Connection Pool:</strong> Reuse HTTPClient across requests; create new instance only if timeout.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Memory Footprint (ESP32-S3)</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>JSON Buffer:</strong> Allocate 4–8 KB DynamicJsonDocument for typical payloads.</li>
        <li><strong>Quote Cache:</strong> Keep last 3–5 quotes in RAM for fast page navigation.</li>
        <li><strong>Free Heap:</strong> Monitor with <code>ESP.getFreeHeap()</code>; restart if &lt; 50 KB free.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Power Consumption</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Active (WiFi + Display):</strong> ~150–250 mA.</li>
        <li><strong>Display Only (WiFi off):</strong> ~50–100 mA.</li>
        <li><strong>Sleep Mode (Deep Sleep):</strong> ~100 µA (wake on GPIO interrupt).</li>
      </ul>
